[2026-03-16T03:04:43.582Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0147cjcdQDNQjTEbHwJL4mut","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a complete picture. Let me create a comprehensive summary of all the files related to the Login/Register page.\n\n## Summary of Login/Register Page Files\n\nI've found all the files related to the Login/Register page in the AirbnbClone application. Here's the complete structure:\n\n### Main Page Component:\n- **/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/pages/Login.tsx** - The main page component that manages the login/register toggle state and renders either the login or register form\n\n### Sub-Components Used on the Login/Register Page:\n- **/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/components/LoginForm.tsx** - Form component for user login (email-only authentication)\n- **/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/components/RegisterForm.tsx** - Form component for user registration (name and email)\n- **/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/components/AuthToggle.tsx** - Toggle component to switch between login and register modes\n\n### Supporting Infrastructure:\n- **/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/slices/authSlice.ts** - Redux slice handling authentication state and async thunks (`loginUser`, `registerUser`, etc.)\n- **/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/store.ts** - Redux store configuration that includes the auth reducer\n- **/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/App.tsx** - Router configuration showing the `/login` route mapped to the Login component\n\n### Routing:\nThe Login page is accessed via the `/login` route and is automatically displayed when an unauthenticated user tries to access the app. Users who are already logged in are redirected to the home page.\n\n### Component Hierarchy:\n```\nLogin (page)\n├── LoginForm (conditional render based on mode)\n├── RegisterForm (conditional render based on mode)\n└── AuthToggle (always renders)\n```\n\nAll authentication state is managed through Redux with localStorage persistence for the current user session."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a69cb5812d057855c (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 25990\ntool_uses: 15\nduration_ms: 16077</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"787afa2e-d7a6-4fb6-9e6b-c697ce29f4b8","uuid":"5ff75b41-2db4-46ae-a1bf-27097507b5b4","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Find all files related to the Login/Register page in /repo/apps/AirbnbClone/. I need the main page component and any sub-components used on that page. Search for files with \"login\", \"register\", \"auth\" in their names under the src directory. Also check for a pages directory structure. Be thorough - look at the routing to understand which components make up the login/register page.","agentId":"a69cb5812d057855c","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a complete picture. Let me create a comprehensive summary of all the files related to the Login/Register page.\n\n## Summary of Login/Register Page Files\n\nI've found all the files related to the Login/Register page in the AirbnbClone application. Here's the complete structure:\n\n### Main Page Component:\n- **/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/pages/Login.tsx** - The main page component that manages the login/register toggle state and renders either the login or register form\n\n### Sub-Components Used on the Login/Register Page:\n- **/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/components/LoginForm.tsx** - Form component for user login (email-only authentication)\n- **/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/components/RegisterForm.tsx** - Form component for user registration (name and email)\n- **/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/components/AuthToggle.tsx** - Toggle component to switch between login and register modes\n\n### Supporting Infrastructure:\n- **/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/slices/authSlice.ts** - Redux slice handling authentication state and async thunks (`loginUser`, `registerUser`, etc.)\n- **/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/store.ts** - Redux store configuration that includes the auth reducer\n- **/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/App.tsx** - Router configuration showing the `/login` route mapped to the Login component\n\n### Routing:\nThe Login page is accessed via the `/login` route and is automatically displayed when an unauthenticated user tries to access the app. Users who are already logged in are redirected to the home page.\n\n### Component Hierarchy:\n```\nLogin (page)\n├── LoginForm (conditional render based on mode)\n├── RegisterForm (conditional render based on mode)\n└── AuthToggle (always renders)\n```\n\nAll authentication state is managed through Redux with localStorage persistence for the current user session."}],"totalDurationMs":16077,"totalTokens":25990,"totalToolUseCount":15,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1134,"cache_read_input_tokens":24381,"output_tokens":470,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1134},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
